#!/bin/sh
#
# Configured as part of the DigitalOcean 1-Click Image build process

myip=$(hostname -I | awk '{print$1}')
cat <<EOM
********************************************************************************

Welcome to the GAIA 1-Click Droplet.

Finish setup in your browser: http://$myip/setup
  * Create the admin account, then paste one AI provider key (OpenAI works).
  * First boot pulls the images; if the page is not up yet, follow
    /var/log/gaia-install.log.

On the server, as the gaia user (sudo -iu gaia):
  * gaia status    - every service and dependency
  * gaia doctor    - what is broken and how to fix it
  * gaia update    - move to the release your CLI ships
  * HTTPS on your own domain: gaia up --domain gaia.example.com

The UFW firewall allows only 22 (SSH), 80 (HTTP) and 443 (HTTPS).

Docs: https://docs.heygaia.io/self-hosting/overview

********************************************************************************
To delete this message of the day: rm -rf $(readlink -f "${0}")
EOM
